## Interface: 16001
## Title: Navigation
## Notes: Sane UI's map. Move the mouse into the screen's top right corner and the map fills the screen: drag it, zoom it with the mouse wheel, and choose between Blizzard's maps, the terrain, or both laid over each other. Esc or the corner again closes it. Being built: the game's own minimap and map stay as they are.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Map_01
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its settings and the command. First: the other files add to that table.
Navigation.lua
# The map's spaces: map, world, the plane it is drawn in; the terrain's grid. Knows no frames
Coords.lua
# Where a view looks: its middle, its zoom, the drag and the wheel. Knows no frames
Camera.lua
# The frame the map is drawn in: its layers, the mouse, what is in view
Canvas.lua
# The terrain: the game's minimap textures, tile by tile
Terrain.lua
# Blizzard's map art: the continent's, and the zone's up close
Art.lua
# The window: docked in the top right corner, the map when it fills the screen, the view buttons
Window.lua
